bug_report:
Another missing Fre from a copy
Testcase:
```

struct s1
{
  int t;
};

struct s2
{
  struct s1 t;
};

int f1(int a)
{
  s1 t{a};
  s2 tt{t};
  s2 ttt = tt;
  s1 *t0 = &ttt.t;
  return t0->t;
}

int f2(int a)
{
  s1 t{a};
  s2 tt{t};
  s2 ttt = tt;
  return ttt.t.t;
}
```

Compile with `-O2 -fno-tree-sra` and see that f1 is not able to optimize to just `return a`. While f2 is.
The only difference between the two at fre1 is:
  _7 = MEM[(struct s1 *)&ttt].t;
vs:
  _6 = ttt.t.t;

Noticed this while looking intoPR 92811if we disable SRA.
